cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or dataset, please cite the thesis below."
title: "Proprioceptive estimation of forearm roll during robotic grasping — code and data"
abstract: >-
  Code and datasets for estimating the human forearm roll angle (pronosupination,
  q5) from the proprioceptive state of an under-actuated robotic gripper grasping
  the forearm: contact-polygon construction from phalange encoders, morphological
  erosion, maximum-area inscribed ellipse (John ellipse / MVIE) and a flexible
  anatomical ellipse fit, forearm-axis reconstruction and q5 computation.
  Supports Sections 2.3 and 3.4 and Experiments 2–3 of the Master's thesis.
